        ConfigOption(key: "env.MADEIRA_CTX_CPU_AREA", title: "Cross-thread GetThreadContext from the x64 snapshot", kind: .choice, defaultValue: "", category: "Exceptions & threads", note: "Another thread's GetThreadContext when the server has no control registers for it. Unset or 0 (default): off; the answer is the server's registers. 1 (upstream's opt-in): the control registers (Pc/Sp/Fp/Lr) from the thread's last exit from emulated code. 2: also the integer registers the caller asked for, and Cpsr 0, from the same snapshot; madeira-bcd's default behaviour, which every game list sets (Ghost of Tsushima's loading screen froze without it). The snapshot is where the thread last left emulated code, not where it is now: a context written back moves the thread back there.", choices: [("", "Off (default)"), ("1", "Control registers"), ("2", "Control and integer registers")], sources: ["build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c"]),
