        ConfigOption(key: "env.MADEIRA_EC_NATIVE_CHILD", title: "Start aarch64 programs in a 64-bit x86 session", kind: .bool, defaultValue: "0", category: "Wine core (ntdll)", note: "ml2280: off (default): an aarch64 program (services.exe, cmd.exe, conhost.exe) started in a session whose first program is 64-bit x86 (ARM64EC) is refused and CreateProcess fails at once. The session's ntdll loads the emulator into it and its threads have no CPU area, so it crashed at its first executable allocation and its exception path faulted until the storm handler ended it (testers' log, 2026-10-28: services.exe started on demand for a launcher installer, twice, 20 s each). A game that needs one starts in the Wine desktop. 1: starts them anyway; MADEIRA_EC_CONHOST=1 still lets conhost.exe through.", choices: [], sources: ["build/ntdll-unix/process_ios.c"]),
        ConfigOption(key: "env.MADEIRA_ECO_NATIVE", title: "Runtime helper threads on efficiency cores", kind: .bool, defaultValue: "0", category: "Wine core (ntdll)", note: "1: the JIT-pool warmer (page warming and the periodic memory walks) and the stale-pointer healer run at utility QoS, on the efficiency cores, ECO on or off; neither does work a frame waits for. The wineserver thread, the exception thread, audio and the interface keep their QoS. Off (default): they keep the QoS they were created with. Read at session start.", choices: [], sources: ["build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c", "build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c", "build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c"]),
